<title>USA: Intelligent Electronics sells unit.</title>
<headline>Intelligent Electronics sells unit.</headline>
<dateline>EXTON, Pa. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intelligent Electronics Inc. said on Tuesday it has signed a definitive agreement to sell the majority of XLSource, its direct computer sales operations to General Electric Capital Information Technology Solutions .</p>
<p>In addition, XLConnect Solutions Inc, IE's 80 percent-owned internetworking professional services subsidiary, has agreed to sell to GE Capital I.T. Solutions certain related contracts and assets.</p>
<p>The total purchase price is about $136 million in cash with IE retaining certain liabilities.</p>
<p>The company said the deal is expected to be completed by mid-July. The transaction has already received anti-trust clearance, it said.</p>
<p>(-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610)</p>
